<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chanda Sahib</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1752">1752</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chanda Sahib was a commander of the Nawab of the Carnatic who seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiruchirappalli">Tiruchirappalli</a> in the 1730s. Captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> in 1741, he was released and with French backing became Nawab of the Carnatic in 1749. British support for his rival Muhammad Ali led to the Siege of Trichinopoly, and he was executed in 1752.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chanda-sahib.jpg" alt="Chanda Sahib" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: T. H. Mannerhow Illustrated by Allan Stewart · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WAR_ELEPHANTS_CHARGE_THE_GATES_OF_THE_FORT_AT_ARCOT..gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
